8. Project development – step by step
Do not try to implement all the modules at once.
1. Step 1 – Project setup
   
   Create Spring Boot project, configure Maven, connect MySQL, run the application.
2. Step 2 – Entity creation
   
   Create User, Product, Category, Order, OrderItem and Payment entities.
3. Step 3 – CRUD operations
   
   Develop create, read, update and delete APIs.
4. Step 4 – Database relationships
   
   Implement one-to-one, one-to-many and many-to-one relationships.
5. Step 5 – Service layer
   
   Implement business logic, DTOs and validation.
6. Step 6 – Security
   
   Implement registration, login, password hashing, JWT and admin/user roles.
7. Step 7 – Ordering functionality
   
   Implement cart, order placement, total calculation and order status management.
8. Step 8 – Payment integration
   
   Integrate a payment gateway using its test environment and verify payment callbacks.
9. Step 9 – Spring AI
   
   Add AI-based menu recommendations and a canteen FAQ assistant.
10. Step 10 – Testing and deployment
    
    Test APIs, write unit and integration tests, document APIs and deploy with Docker.
